## 5. Rollout Phases & Backward Compatibility

Deploying the Interruptible Agentic Control Plane across heterogeneous distributed clusters follows a strict four-phase migration schedule:

- **Phase 1: Shadow Telemetry & Instrumentation.** Deploy `AgentControlBlock` wrappers into staging agent environments with logging-only mode enabled. Measure interception latency and verify zero performance regression in tool execution loops.
- **Phase 2: Cooperative Pause Activation.** Enable user-space `assert_execution_validity()` checks across all active agent runtimes. Validate that orchestrator pause commands successfully freeze agent tool-calling loops within 5ms.
- **Phase 3: Kernel-Enforced Guard Rails.** Attach eBPF SECCOMP and tracepoint filters to production worker nodes. Enforce hard syscall blocking upon receipt of `AGENT_EXEC_ABORT` signals.
- **Phase 4: Full Autonomous Mesh Interconnect.** Deprecate legacy polling mechanisms and mandate cryptographically signed control frames across all multi-tenant agent deployments.

