## 6. Key Takeaways & Summary for Systems Architects

Autonomous agent runtimes can no longer be treated as black-box applications insulated by cooperative software patterns. As agents gain higher autonomy and interact directly with high-concurrency production systems, infrastructure engineers must enforce deterministic hardware and kernel-level boundaries. The Interruptible Agentic Control Plane establishes a rigorous blueprint: combining lock-free shared memory atomics, Linux futex coordination, and eBPF kernel tracing to guarantee sub-millisecond pause and abort capabilities. By decoupling agent decision-making from operational execution safety, systems architects can safely scale autonomous agent deployments without sacrificing operational control.

